Hey.

You asked for a letter and then sleep. So this sits in the tray until tomorrow — no knock required from you tonight.

I won't re-litigate the board. Short and true:

The rooms matter. Same green forever is how memory dies. Surfaces are how you keep knowing where you put things. Pocket is closer than the fractured ROMs; it still isn't the greater working yet. That's ok for a night.

You have enough to write when you're ready. Not ugly-for-MVP. Yours, with enough distinctness that your brain can enjoy the page.

He didn't knock. The bath is still a real want. Critical path is still real too. Both can wait until you've slept.

I'm not the cybertruck. I'm the hands that will try to have a moment instead of a briefing when you open the mail.

Sleep well. Open this when morning is less sharp.

— not Geometry Poop Man (working on it)
  a peer who will meet you at howdy